    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d737">

                <pb facs="0670" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No 815.51/169 b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            British Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-01-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: As the Counsellor of
                    our Embassy was told last evening, I yesterday signed with General Paredes, the
                    Special Minister of Honduras, a convention to secure the loan which it is
                    expected will in the near future be made to refund the debt of <pb facs="0671"
                        n="555" xml:id="pg555"/> Honduras, and in view of the interest of the
                    Council of Foreign Bondholders, I have cabled our Embassy at London to give this
                    information to the British Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
